<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0000303" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Conversion therapy" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Reparative therapy" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Reorientation therapy" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sexual reorientation therapy" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Efforts to change the sexual or gender identity of an individual who is or is suspected to be LGBTQ+ to meet heterosexual or cisgender norms, typically under the belief that being LGBTQ+ is dangerous and/or the result of mental illness or trauma. The processes involved in conversion therapy include visualization training, spiritual interventions, and other aversion treatments. " .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000106> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003512> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006004076> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/sexualReorientation> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2019-05-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
