<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Differences in sex development" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Divergences in sex development" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DSDs" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hermaphroditism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Intersexuality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Variations in sex development" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "VSDs" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Intersexual" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An umbrella term used to refer to people born with variations in their physical sex characteristics--including genitals, gonads, chromosomes, and hormonal factors--that do not fit typical definitions of male or female bodies." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Un término general utilizado para referirse a personas que nacen con variaciones en sus características sexuales físicas (incluidos genitales, gónadas, cromosomas y factores hormonales) que no se ajustan a las definiciones típicas de cuerpos masculinos o femeninos." .
