<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0000366" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Drab (LGBTQ+ culture)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Drab (cultura LGBTQ+)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Drab" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Slang term used to describe people wearing masculine clothing, typically drag queens or crossdressers who also sometimes wear feminine clothing. Drab is a shortened form of the phrase \"dressed as a boy\" or \"dress resembling a boy.\"" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término de la jerga utilizado para describir a personas que visten ropa masculina, generalmente drag queens o transformistas que a veces también visten ropa femenina. Drab es una forma abreviada de la frase en inglés \"dressed as a boy\" o \"dress resembling a boy\"." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000568> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000366> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000289> .
