<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Drag balls" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Bailes de drag" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Drag balls" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Balls de drag" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Events that are part of the drag ball subculture that emerged in early 20th-century New York City among primarily African-American and Latin American LGBTQ+ people. During a drag ball, individuals \"walk\" or perform for prizes." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Eventos que forman parte de la subcultura de bailes de drag que surgió a principios del siglo XX en la ciudad de Nueva York entre personas LGBTQ+ principalmente afroamericanas y latinoamericanas. Durante un drag ball, las personas \"caminan\" o actúan para ganar premios." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000368> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000861> .
