<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Œstromania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Oversexuality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Satyrism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Satyromania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sexual hyperesthesia" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sexual hyperversion" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe a level or frequency of sexual desire that is perceived as excessive within a given culture. Though the medical community has not reached a consensus as to whether hypersexuality should be included as a clinical diagnosis, doctors and psychologists have historically diagnosed LGBTQ+ people with hypersexuality (or other related labels) in order to wrongly treat their identities and desires as medical disorders. Should only be used in a historical context or if an individual self-identifies with the term." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término utilizado para describir un nivel o una frecuencia de deseo sexual que se percibe como excesiva dentro de una cultura determinada. Aunque la comunidad médica no ha llegado a un consenso sobre si la hipersexualidad debe incluirse como diagnóstico clínico, históricamente los médicos y psicólogos han diagnosticado a personas LGBTQ+ con hipersexualidad (u otras etiquetas relacionadas) para tratar erróneamente sus identidades y deseos como trastornos médicos. Utilícese únicamente en un contexto histórico o si una persona se identifica con el término." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001284> .
