<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/intersexConditions> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2019-05-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0000670" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Intersex genital mutilation" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Mutilación genital intersex" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "IGM" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mutilación genital a personas intersex" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Surgeries or other medical treatments performed, typically on newborn babies or children, to \"normalize\" the patient's reproductive or sexual anatomy and force their body to conform to medical or social expectations for what is male or female. IGM practices can be performed for cultural, social, or religious reasons. Though they are typically justified through a medical lens, IGM practices are medically unnecessary and non-consensual." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cirugías u otros tratamientos médicos realizados, generalmente en  recién nacidos y niños, para \"normalizar\" la anatomía sexual o reproductiva del paciente y obligar a su cuerpo a acomodarse a las expectativas médicas o sociales de lo que es masculino o femenino. Las prácticas de MGI se pueden realizar por razones culturales, sociales o religiosas. Aunque normalmente se justifican desde una perspectiva médica, las prácticas de MGI son médicamente innecesarias y no consensuadas." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000281> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002847> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000352> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000618> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000666> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000670> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000673> .
