<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001116" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Pink triangles" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Triángulos rosas" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Triángulos rosados" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "International symbol of gay pride and the gay rights movement that symbolizes the reclamation of the pink triangles used in Nazi Germany to identify gay men (and, later, bisexual men and transgender women) who were sent to concentration camps." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Símbolo internacional del orgullo gay y del movimiento por los derechos gay que simboliza la reclamación de los triángulos rosas utilizados en la Alemania nazi para identificar a los hombres gay (y, eventualmente, a los hombres bisexuales y las mujeres transgénero) que fueron enviados a campos de concentración." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000954> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000954> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/pinkTriangles> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2019-05-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001116> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001117" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Pinkwashing" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lavado rosa" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lavado de imagen rosa" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A variety of marketing and political strategies aimed at promoting products, countries, people, or entities to LGBTQ+ people; using LGBTQ+-related symbols in order to be perceived as progressive, modern, and tolerant; and/or utilizing concern for LGBTQ+ people and rights to justify or deviate attention from settler-colonialism, genocide, invasion, and intervention in other countries." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001117> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Una variedad de estrategias políticas y de marketing destinada a promover productos, países, personas o entidades entre personas LGBTQ+ o utilizar símbolos LGBTQ+ para ser percibidos como progresistas, modernos y tolerantes." .
