<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001255> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001255> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001255> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001256" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Saris" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In Jewish culture, this term is used to refer to individuals who were assigned male at birth but later developed feminine characteristics." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "En la cultura judía, este término se utiliza para referirse a personas a quienes se les asignó al sexo masculino al nacer pero que luego desarrollaron características femeninas." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/saris> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2019-05-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-03-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001256> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
