<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Tumtum" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term originating in Rabbinic Judaism to refer to someone with an unknown sex; literally translates to \"hidden.\" Used historically to refer to intersex variations where the genitals were covered by skin. Only use for individuals who are Jewish and who self-identify as Tumtum." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término hebreo utilizado en referencia a un género desconocido; se traduce literalmente como \"oculto\"." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001477> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560> .
