<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001538" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Erotomania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Erotomanía" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Clinical erotomania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "De Clérambault syndrome" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "De Clérambault's syndrome" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Obsessional erotomania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Primary erotomania" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Erotomanía clínica" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Síndrome de De Clérambault" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Erotomanía obsesiva" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Erotomanía primaria" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Condition characterized by an individual's persistent and often mistaken belief that another person is infatuated or in love with them. Can also be used to describe a level or frequency of sexual desire perceived as excessive within a given culture. Medical doctors and psychologists have historically diagnosed LGBTQ+ people with erotomania in order to wrongly treat their identities and desires as medical disorders. Should only be used in a historical context or if an individual self-identifies with the term." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Condición caracterizada por la creencia persistente y a menudo errónea de una persona de que otra persona está encaprichada o enamorada de él. También se puede utilizar para describir un nivel o una frecuencia de deseo sexual percibida como excesiva dentro de una cultura determinada. Históricamente, los médicos y psicólogos han diagnosticado a las personas LGBTQ+ con erotomanía para erróneamente tratar sus identidades y deseos como trastornos médicos. Utilícese únicamente en un contexto histórico o si una persona se identifica con el término." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000656> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001283> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh97003456> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/erotomania> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2020-06-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001538> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001539" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "LGBTQ+ people with internet sex addictions" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Personas LGBTQ+ con adicciones al sexo por Internet" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "LGBTQ+ people with cybersex addictions" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "LGBTQ+ people with internet sexual addictions" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "LGBTQ+ people with porn addictions" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "LGBTQ+ people with pornography addictions" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "LGBTQ+ people experiencing addiction to or dependency upon sexual activities involving the internet, including watching pornography, engaging in sexual conversations online, etc. Only use to refer to individuals who describe themselves as having internet sex addictions, not individuals who sexual practices are perceived as promiscuous or excessive by others." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Personas LGBTQ+ que experimentan una adicción o dependencia de actividades sexuales que involucran el internet, incluyendo ver pornografía, participar de conversaciones sexuales en línea, etc. Utilícese únicamente para referirse a personas que se describen a sí mismas como adictas al sexo por internet, no a personas cuyas prácticas sexuales se perciban como promiscuas o excesivo por otras personas." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001283> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001539> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> <http://homosaurus.org/v2/internetSexAddiction> .
