<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001656> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001656> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0001657" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Nesting partners" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Compañeros de anidación" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A term used in non-monogamous communities to refer to partners an individual lives with. Often used in place of language that is seen as hierarchical (e.g., primary partner, secondary partner)." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término utilizado en comunidades no monógamas para referirse a las parejas con las que vive una persona. A menudo, se utiliza en lugar de un lenguaje que se considera jerárquico (por ejemplo, \"pareja principal\", \"pareja secundaria\")." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001660> .
