<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Passing (Sexuality)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Passing (sexualidad)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Passing (Sexual identity)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Passing (Sexual orientation)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Pasando" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Pasar desapercibido" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ability of a person who is not heterosexual to \"pass,\" or be accepted or regarded as heterosexual by others. \"Passing\" has historically been used to describe an individual's ability to \"pass\" as a certain race or ethnicity, though the term was later appropriated by the LGBTQ+ community." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "La capacidad de una persona que no es heterosexual de \"pasar\", ser aceptada o considerada heterosexual por otras personas. \"Pasar\" se ha utilizado históricamente para describir la capacidad de una persona de \"pasar\" como una determinada raza o etnia, aunque eventualmente la comunidad LGBTQ+ se apropió del término." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001901> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001090> .
