<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Amor de chicos" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The manga and anime genre of fictional male-male romance created for a primarily female audience; sometimes used interchangeably with \"Yaoi\" in English (but not in Japanese)." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "El género de manga y anime de romance ficticio entre hombres creado para una audiencia principalmente femenina; a veces se utiliza indistintamente con \"Yaoi\" en inglés (pero no en japonés)." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002144> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002218> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003500> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000557> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002153" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Bury your gays" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Dead lesbian syndrome" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The trope in fiction that requires that LGBTQ+ characters die or meet some other type of unhappy ending. The trope is also known as \"dead lesbian syndrome\" due to the tendency for lesbian characters and bisexual female characters to be the targets. Transgender characters have also often been subjected to this trope." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "El tropo de ficción que requiere que los personajes LGBTQ+ mueran o tengan otro tipo de final infeliz. El tropo también se conoce como el \"síndrome de lesbiana muerta\" debido a la tendencia de que personajes lésbicos y personajes femeninos bisexuales sean el foco del tropo. Las personajes transgénero a menudo también han sido sometidas a este tropo." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002160> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000443> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002153> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
