<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002176> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002177" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Kirk/Spock" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "K/S" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Spirk" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The homoerotic fan pairing of Kirk and Spock from Star Trek: The Original Series. The Kirk/Spock fandom originated much of the terminology and practices associated with fandom today--for example, the word \"slash\" comes from the forward slash in Kirk/Spock." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "El emparejamiento homoerótico por fans de Kirk y Spock de \"Star Trek: The Original Series\". El fandom de Kirk/Spock originó gran parte de la terminología y las prácticas asociadas con el fandom actual; por ejemplo, la palabra \"slash\" proviene de la barra diagonal en Kirk/Spock." .
