<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002186" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Omegaverse" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Omegaverso" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "A/B/O" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ABO" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Alpha/Beta/Omega" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Omergaverse" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The alternate universe fanworks trope in which society is divided into three categories of people: alphas, betas, and omegas. Fanworks in the omegaverse often depict characters with genitalia and breeding behaviors (such as heat cycles) similar to wolves. Use to describe fanworks in the omegaverse that focus on LGBTQ+ people and issues." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "El tropo de obras de fans del universo alternativo en el que la sociedad se divide en tres categorías de personas: alfas, betas y omegas. Las obras de fans en el omegaverso a menudo representan personajes con genitales y comportamientos reproductivos (como ciclos de celo) similares a los de los lobos. Utilícese para describir obras de fans en el omegaverso que se centran en personas y cuestiones LGBTQ+." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002143> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002184> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002176> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002186> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002187" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "One true pairing" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "OTP" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Slang term referring to a fan's primary \"ship\" or preferred relationship within a fandom." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término de la jerga que se refiere al \"ship\" principal de un fan o a la relación preferida dentro de un fandom. Siglas en inglés para \"una pareja única\" o \"una pareja veradera.\"" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002189> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002187> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002160> .
