<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001101> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002190> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002191" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Queerbaiting" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Queer baiting" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Cebo queer" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marketing tactic in which creators of a piece of media purposefully hint at but do not explicitly depict or follow through with queer relationships or queer representation. Queerbaiting is distinct from queer coding in that queer coding is not typically used as a marketing tactic." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Táctica de marketing en la que los creadores de una pieza mediática insinúan intencionadamente, pero no representan ni dan seguimiento a relaciones o representaciones queer. El queerbaiting se diferencia de la codificación queer en que la codificación queer no suele utilizarse como táctica de marketing." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000899> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002191> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002192" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Queer coding" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Codificación queer" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Queercoding" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purposeful subtextual coding of a character or relationship in a piece of media as queer. Queer coding is distinct from the practice of queerbaiting in that the queer codes are intentionally present rather than falsely implied and are not typically used as a marketing tactic." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Codificación subtextual intencionada de un personaje o de una relación en una pieza mediática como queer. La codificación queer se diferencia de la práctica del queerbaiting en que los códigos queer están presentes intencionalmente en lugar de implícitos falsamente y no suelen utilizarse como táctica de marketing." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000609> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002192> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000972> .
