<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002196" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Real person fiction" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Ficción de personas reales" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "RPF" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "RPS" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Real people fiction" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Real person slash" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Real person stories" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Real person fiction" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fanfiction about real people, such as actors or musicians; often but not always used to describe fanfiction focusing on (real or imagined) same-sex or same-gender relationships between celebrities." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fanfiction sobre personas reales, como actores o músicos; a menudo, pero no siempre, se utiliza para describir fanfiction que se centra en relaciones (reales o imaginarias) entre celebridades del mismo sexo o del mismo género." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002205> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002142> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002147> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002196> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002197" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Seme (Yaoi)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used in yaoi or yaoi fan communities to describe the giving or dominant partner in a fictional male-male relationship." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término utilizado en las comunidades yaoi o de fans del yaoi para describir a la pareja dadivosa o dominante en una relación ficticia entre dos personas masculinas." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002217> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001376> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002151> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002152> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002197> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002198" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Ship names in fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Nombres de ship en el fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Pairing names in fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Ship names en el fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Names used to describe common pairings in fandom. Ship names are often portmanteaus of the names of two (or more) characters in the ship (e.g., Spirk for Spock and Kirk)." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Nombres utilizados para describir emparejamientos comunes en el fandom. Los nombres de los \"ships\" suelen ser combinaciones de los nombres de dos (o más) personajes del \"ship\" (por ejemplo, \"Spirk\" para Spock y Kirk)." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002177> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002199" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Shipping in fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Shippeo en el fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Shipping en el fandom" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe fans' desire to see certain characters in sexual or romantic relationships, as well as the practice of pairing those characters in fanworks. The terms \"shipping\" and \"ship\" come from \"relationship.\"" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término utilizado para describir el deseo de los fans de ver a ciertos personajes en relaciones sexuales o románticas, así como la práctica de emparejar a esos personajes en obras de fans. Los términos \"shipping\" y \"ship\" provienen de \"relationship\" en inglés." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002156> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002189> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002198> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002180> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002199> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002200" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Slash (Genre)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Slash (género)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Slash" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A genre of fanworks in which two or more characters of the same sex or gender are placed in sexual or romantic situations with one another. Slash fanworks are commonly erotic or pornographic. While the term \"slash\" has historically been used for male/male couples only, it has been recently been broadened to include LGBTQ+ relationships other than those between two men." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Un género de obras de fans en el que dos o más personajes del mismo sexo o género son colocados en situaciones sexuales o románticas entre sí. Las obras de fans Slash son comúnmente eróticas o pornográficas. Si bien el término \"slash\" se ha utilizado históricamente solo para relaciones entre hombres, recientemente se ha ampliado para incluir relaciones LGBTQ+ distintas de aquellas entre dos hombres." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002203> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002162> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-07-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002200> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002201" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Slash art" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Arte slash" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Artwork depicting same-sex or same-gender couples that is usually erotic or pornographic in nature. Historically used for male-male couples only, but is now used more broadly; includes femslash art." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Obras de arte que representan parejas del mismo sexo o del mismo género y que suelen ser de naturaleza erótica o pornográfica. Históricamente se utilizaba únicamente para parejas de hombres, pero ahora se utiliza de forma más amplia; incluye arte femslash." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002155> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002204> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000816> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002201> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001345> .
