<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2021008248> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002272" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Womanism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Mujerismo" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Womanist theory" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Teoria mujerista" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A social theory based on the history and everyday experiences of Black women. Womanism grew out of the perceived indifference of the feminist movement towards the needs of Black women, who are often excluded from the categories of \"female\" and \"femininity\" as understood by white feminists. At the core of womanism is the idea that mainstream feminism is a movement led by white women to serve white women's goals, which can be indifferent or even oppositional to the needs of Black women." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Una teoría social basada en la historia y las experiencias cotidianas de las mujeres negras. El mujerismo surgió de la indiferencia percibida del movimiento feminista hacia las necesidades de las mujeres negras, que a menudo están excluidas de las categorías de \"femenino\" y \"feminidad\" tal como las entienden las feministas blancas. Al centro del mujerismo está la idea de que el feminismo dominante es un movimiento liderado por mujeres blancas para servir a los objetivos de las mujeres blancas, que pueden ser indiferentes o incluso opuestos a las necesidades de las mujeres negras." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000667> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002038> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002270> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002271> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003176> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006001576> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002272> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002273" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "QTPOC" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Queer and trans people of color" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Personas queer y trans de color" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Acronym used to refer to queer and trans people of color as a group. Typically used to acknowledge the particularities of queer and trans people of color's experiences and the intersections of queerphobia, transphobia, and racism as directed towards queer and trans people of color." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Acrónimo utilizado para referirse a personas de color queer y trans como grupo. Normalmente se utiliza para reconocer las particularidades de las experiencias de las personas queer y trans de color y las intersecciones de la queerfobia, la transfobia y el racismo dirigidas hacia las personas queer y trans de color." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001892> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001928> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001101> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002273> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002274" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Transfeminism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Transfeminismo" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Trans feminism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Trans feminismo" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "As defined by Emi Koyama, transfeminism is a movement by and for trans woman who view the liberation of trans women as essential to the liberation of all women." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Como lo define Emi Koyama, el transfeminismo es un movimiento por y para mujeres trans que ven la liberación de las mujeres trans como esencial para la liberación de todas las mujeres." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000667> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001642> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001892> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-28"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002274> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002275" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Third-wave feminism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Feminismo de la tercera ola" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Third wave feminism" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Period of feminist political activity beginning in the early 1990s that embraced diversity and individualism in women and sought to redefine what it meant to be a feminist. The third wave is characterized by the emergence of new feminist movements and theories such as intersectionality, sex positivity, ecofeminism, transfeminism, and postmodern feminism." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Periodo de actividad política feminista que comenzó a principios de la década de 1990 y que abrazó la diversidad y el individualismo de las mujeres y buscó redefinir lo que significaba ser feminista. La tercera ola se caracteriza por el surgimiento de nuevos movimientos y teorías feministas como la interseccionalidad, la positividad sexual, el ecofeminismo, el transfeminismo y el feminismo posmoderno." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003174> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008001561> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000437> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002275> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002276" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Sapphic identity" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Identidad sáfica" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sapphist identity" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Identidad safista" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sexual identity or sexuality term used to describe women and, in some definitions, non-binary people who are sapphic, or attracted to women. Only use to describe individuals who describe their identity as sapphic." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término de identidad sexual o de sexualidad utilizado para describir a mujeres y, en algunas definiciones, a personas no binarias que son sáficas o que se ven atraídas por mujeres. Utilícese únicamente para describir a personas que describen su identidad como sáfica." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001295> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001295> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002277" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Sapphics" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Sáficas" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sapphists" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Personas sáficas" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Women and, in some definitions, non-binary people of any sexual identity or sexuality who are attracted to women. Some but not all sapphics use the term \"sapphic\" to describe their sexual identity or sexuality. Only use to describe individuals who self-identify as sapphic." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mujeres y, en algunas definiciones, personas no binarias de cualquier identidad sexual o sexualidad que se sientan atraídas por mujeres. Algunas pero no todas las personas sáficas utilizan el término \"sáfica\" para describir su identidad sexual o sexualidad. Utilícese únicamente para describir a personas que se identifican como sáficas." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001297> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002276> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85117455> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002277> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002278" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "MLM (Men Loving Men)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Man loving man" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Men loving men" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hombres que aman hombres" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Slang term used to describe men who have romantic and/or sexual relationships with other men; often used as an alternative to the term \"Men who have sex with men.\" Can be used to describe men who are exclusively or primarily interested in men, as well as men who are also interested in people of other or all genders. Only use to describe people who self-identify as MLM." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término de la jerga utilizado para describir a hombres que tienen relaciones románticas y/o sexuales con otros hombres; a menudo se utiliza como alternativa al término \"Hombres que tienen sexo con hombres\". Puede utilizarse para describir a hombres que están interesados ​​exclusiva o principalmente en hombres, así como a hombres que también están interesados ​​en personas de otros o todos los géneros. Utilícese únicamente para describir a las personas que se autoidentifiquen como MLM." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001008> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001297> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000365> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001254> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000915> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022-11-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002278> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0002279" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "WLW (Women Loving Women)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "WLW (Mujeres que aman mujeres)" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Woman loving woman" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Women loving women" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mujeres amando mujeres" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mujeres amando a mujeres" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Slang term used to describe women who have romantic and/or sexual relationships with other women. Can be used to describe women who are exclusively or primarily interested in women, as well as women who are also interested in people of other or all genders. Only use to describe people who self-identify as WLW." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0002279> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Término de la jerga utilizado para describir a mujeres que tienen relaciones románticas y/o sexuales con otras mujeres. Puede utilizarse para describir a mujeres que están exclusiva o principalmente interesadas en mujeres, así como a mujeres que también están interesadas en personas de otros o todos los géneros. Utilícese únicamente para describir a personas que se identifiquen como WLW." .
