<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003974> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003974" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003974> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Warmipangui" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003974> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Amongst the Canelos-Quichua, one of the indigenous Kichwa peoples of the Ecuadorian Amazon, this term is used to refer to people who were assigned male at birth but have the ability to transition between feminine and masculine. " .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003974> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003974> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003293> .
