<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003984" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Transmedicalists" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Truscum" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Individuals who believe that being transgender is primarily a medical issue and that gender dysphoria and the desire to medically transition are both necessary to be considered \"truly\" transgender." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003910> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000567> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v4> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003984> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003985" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Chrononormativity" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Normative time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe the ways in which human lives and experiences are expected to follow specific, linear patterns over time in conformity with normative frameworks. This includes expectations regarding how long and what hours people work, with the aim of achieving maximum productivity, as well as expectations for people to reach life milestones, such as graduating high school, getting married, and having children, at specific ages and in a particular order." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001323> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001323> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v4> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003986" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Crip time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Crip temporality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe the ways in which disabled and chronically ill people experience and relate to time differently than is socially expected. According to Alison Kafer, quoted in a paper published by Ellen Samuels, \"rather than bend disabled bodies and minds to meet the clock, crip time bends the clock to meet disabled bodies and minds.\"" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001891> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001317> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v4> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003986> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003987" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Queer time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Queer temporality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe the ways in which queer people experience and relate to time differently than is socially expected. This may include delayed or non-linear development before coming out, disrupted life trajectories, and a sense of impending mortality, particularly during the AIDS epidemic. " .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001219> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v4> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003987> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003988" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "White time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "White temporality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "White temporal imaginary" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Racialization of time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Racial time" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term used to describe the racialization of time in a white supremacist society, which results in unequal temporal access to institutions, resources, power, etc. This term also references the ways in which non-white people are expected to conform to specific, linear patterns over time, as well as the calculation of time and history through white, Western expectations for progress and productivity." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003985> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001902> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001323> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-04-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v4> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003988> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "Version 4.1.0" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003989" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Compulsory heterosexuality" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Comphet" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Term coined by Adrienne Rich in 1980 to describe the idea that heterosexuality is assumed of and enforced upon people in patriarchal societies to ensure the continued subjugation of women. Thus, heterosexuality and, particularly, women's sexual interest in men, is not always natural but instead is ingrained as a social requirement from an early age." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001323> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001365> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0003989> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000619> .
